  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fair Finance Sida FFA II Vietnam_LACEM</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Financial inclusion plays an important role in eradicating poverty and reducing inequality in society. Promoting financial literacyis an important part of the Comprehensive Financial Strategy promulgated by the Government of Viet Nam. One of the tasks and solutions mentioned in the strategy is to promote educational communication programs, disseminate financial knowledge to the people, develop and implement programs to provide information for people to understand the benefits, costs, etc  risks and methods of managing and effectively using financial products and services. Thus, the content of financial knowledge that people need to understand clearlyis about financial products and services to use in accordance with their needs and abilities and at the same time be able to decideto use financial services effectively that can avoid risks in the process of using financial services.  ensuring fairness and towards sustainable development.
The initiative was implemented on 4 communes of Le Thuy district, Quang Binh province, including:
- NganThuy commune is a mountainous commune in Le Thuy district, Quang Binh with 6 villages/hamlets with 683 households with 2,705 people(2023) with about 65% of ethnic minorities and 50% of poor and near-poor households.
- Lam Thuy commune is a border mountainous commune with 6 villages, about 500 households, 1200 households, 70% of whom are ethnic minorities and 70% of whom are poor and near-poor households.
- Kim Thuy commune is a border mountainous commune, with 12 villages and hamlets of about 600 households, 1400 households, 75% of whom are ethnic minorities and 70% of whom are poor and near-poor households.
- Hoa Thuy commune is a delta commune consisting of 10 villages with about 3000 households, 8000 households with 20% of whom are poor and near-poor households.</narrative>
  </description>
